//! Mathematical functions over semantic Core Numbers.

/// Answers the principal square root of `value`, which must be a semantic
/// Number: an Integer, a Fraction, a Float, or a Complex. Any other argument
/// signals an Error; no argument is converted and no message is sent to it.
///
/// A rational root of an exact value is exact (`sqrt(1/4)` is `1/2`); an
/// irrational one is a Float computed from the exact value. A negative real
/// gives a Complex (`sqrt(-4)` is `Complex(0, 2)`, `sqrt(-4.0)` is
/// `Complex(+0.0, +2.0)`). NaN, infinities, signed zeros, overflow, and
/// underflow never signal an Error; a Float-bearing Complex follows the
/// principal-branch special-value rules of `std:math/Math`.
sqrt: ((facility) => (value) => {
    facility.sqrt(value)
})(_mathSqrtFacility)

// The runtime-provisioned facility is captured privately above; it is not
// module surface.
context.removeSlot("_mathSqrtFacility")
